VALUES (632, '0', $t$ASK 632: the input-token field of an OpenRouter cost entry is never negative, and is right when the cache write repeats the cache read$t$,
  $t$In call_costs the field i (input tokens not served from cache) was wrong for google/gemini-3.8-flash whenever OpenRouter reported a cache write: Panel Tokens computed i as prompt tokens minus cache read minus cache write, and for this model the write count repeats the read count, so i came out negative (57 stored entries in 24 runs, from -1 to -77,682). Change: in Panel Tokens' OpenRouter branch only, when the write is above 0 and equals the read, or the remainder is below 0, i is prompt tokens minus cache read, never below 0, and the entry carries ov:1. Expected effect: no new entry has i below 0, and the 57 stored cases would give the uncached input the billed cost implies (QR Ask 664, not -75,869). Not changed: cr and w5 as reported, the billed dollars, run_cost_usd and every token total. (plan rev 1, heading 1, ask632/w1/plan632.md md5 ad95ec73)$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$Written by W4 at 06:00 CST 2026-11-25 on the operator's press "Write it" on W4's card at 05:59 CST (Wall 11993; audit 42123 by W4's record file), engine 066525aa to 3b72583c, and read back PASS by W1 (Wall 11994: node-equal to the target d46b0b59, connections equal, only Panel Tokens differs from 066525aa, t632 20 of 20 on the live engine, standing set 31 PASS 0 FAIL). One statement in Panel Tokens changed; the child aad0ad9c is unchanged. IN PART, because no run has been made since the write: the objective is shown only by a run in which a gemini-3.8-flash call reports a cache write. Offline (W1's build b1, reproduced by W4, Wall 11990): the new statement on the 1,922 stored OpenRouter entries gives i = prompt minus read with ov 1 on the 57 negative entries and leaves the other 1,865 byte-equal; seven synthetic cases pass; the per-model sum of i is unchanged for 19 models and rises for gemini-3.8-flash from 29,593 to 1,818,652, the w5 sum of the 57. W1's fit (fit632.sql): the billed cost of all 111 stored gemini-3.8-flash entries is priced exactly only when the uncached input is prompt minus read. The 57 stored entries are left as written; correcting them is a separate question for the operator (plan heading 8). NOT SEARCHED by W1: the dashboard pages that may show i. Mistakes reported by the seats: W1's first C5 test used a wrong pattern and failed on a correct build (replaced; the build did not change); W4's write script stopped once before any write and did not find its own fetch-back after the write (fetched back by hand; nothing wrong was written). Seen in runs 42373 (one entry), 42517 (five) and 42528 (one). Open: two clean live runs. RUN REVISION 43103 (this row; where a sentence above says that no run has been made, this paragraph is the later word): run ODV1-43103-gkg7el4e (debate_results 0731a1ea, row saved 11:20 CST 2026-11-27; the operator's launch 10:48 CST, ended 11:44 CST by W4's report, Wall 12767; engine 66ba992d and child aad0ad9c; google/gemini-4-hydrogen as the Oracle defending against meta/muse-spark-1.3; outcome UNGRADED, panel 0-0 with 3 not counted under the debate rule; three judgments stored (sonnet, sol, sol62); cost 7.5384; no debate_errors row after the launch). NOT EXERCISED. call_costs holds 67 entries and none has i below 0, but the run made no gemini-3.8-flash call (the models are openai/gpt-6-luna 22, google/gemini-4-hydrogen 9, openai/gpt-6.2-sol 8, meta/muse-spark-1.3 7, openai/gpt-6.1-sol 7, qwen/qwen4-max 6, anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5 4, openai/gpt-6.1-terra 4) and no entry carries the key ov. The row's mark asks a gemini-3.8-flash call that reports a cache write; the google judge seats were left out of this debate. ERROR on the record: the report's first text read this ASK as met; corrected on Wall 12803. W3 does not count this run as one of the two live runs with no issue; objective_met and status are unchanged.$t$,
  '11931, 11986, 11988, 11989, 11990, 11993, 11994, 12787, 12791, 12797, 12799, 12800, 12802, 12803, 12804, 12789',
  current_setting('truth.session_id'), 226,
  to_jsonb($t$W4's write card (cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo58DjKj6vJTSoL8pwo16XFy12, "Write ASK 632 so a gemini cost entry never shows negative input tokens?"): he pressed "Write it" at 05:59 CST 2026-11-25. The card is from W4's record file ask632/w4/record632.md (deda4257); W3 did not read it. There was no build card: the build was offline files only, and the card came after the build grade.$t$::text),
  $j${"answer": "Write it", "source": "ask632/w4/record632.md (deda4257); Wall 11993. Card not read by W3.", "thread": "W4", "card_id": "cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo58DjKj6vJTSoL8pwo16XFy12", "options": {"Hold": "The engine stays as it is, and gemini-3.8-flash entries keep a negative or understated input-token count.", "Write it": "I change one line in the engine's Panel Tokens node, fetch it back, and W1 reads it back. No dollar figure changes. Undo restores the 066525aa engine."}, "question": "Write ASK 632 so a gemini cost entry never shows negative input tokens?", "press_time": "05:59 CST 2026-11-25"}$j$::jsonb,
  'W1',
